{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1515391-shifters-before-humanity","id":1515391,"title":"Shifters before humanity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-17T10:01:41-07:00","id":1515391,"title":"Shifters before humanity","content":"We know were-shifters have existed long before humanity did thank to the ananasi and mokole, but what did primal fera &quot;Shift&quot; into? For example: would a theoretical Pre-humanity Garou only have lupus and hispo? Did the Ancient Ananasi only have swarm and Big Spider form?<br /> <br /> What ultimately caused the sudden need for every fera to be human-compatible? What made the funny monkeys so suddenly important to the great, sapient shaman-beasts of the ancient times?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T10:44:04-07:00","id":1515403,"title":"","content":"They might also have Crinos; Mokole surely would have had access to their Archid forms even during the time after their Drachid kin died but before they took on human forms. As for what was suddenly so important, my guess would be a single point mutation on interleukin-1 receptor like protein, which is associated with the leap from archaic <i>Homo sapiens</i> with fewer basal radioglia (neuron precursors) to modern <i>Homo sapiens sapiens</i>, which has a waste of riches in the same and underwent a sudden improvement in tool development, likely among other cultural changes. The Kings probably had a similar experience in some ways, back when the Drachid form was still a twinkle in the eye (Mokole are said to be even older than them, but any lineages that recall anything before the Triassic died out in the War of Rage).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T11:19:14-07:00","id":1515406,"title":"","content":"The<b> Insect Races</b>, the <b>Mokol\u00e9</b> and the <b>Rokea</b> not had &quot;homid&quot; , for obvious reasons...<br /> The Mokol\u00e9 after the Lizard Kings (dinosaurs, plesiosaurs, and pterosaurs) re-rolled to Humans<br /> The Drachid form was the near-human form of the Fera before the evolution of hominids - Some believe that the Drachids were the blueprint from which Gaia would derive the idea of humanity.<br /> They were basically Saurian of Dr. Who (and other works) and in theory been able to crossbreed with others, not just the Kings - but only the Ananasi used it really<br /> <br /> During the Age of Kings there lived <b>Ammonite shifters</b> (who were at war with the Rokea and folk became extinct along with their animal kin in the Wonder Work) and <b>Bristlecreeper shifters</b> (whatever a bristlecreeper<i> is</i> ) according Breedbook: Mokol\u00e9 and Rokea<br /> The Rokea say that millions of years ago they were at war with giant, mobile, <b>shapeshifting sea anemones called Qyrall</b>, who served Qyrl (They would ride the leviathans and use Qyrl's gifts of stealth to block out the massive brutes' presence until they were right on top of a slew, then change in to an <i>almost-humanoid</i> shape to do battle\u200b)<br /> The Rokea defeated and apparently eradicated them<br /> <br /> These probably had homid, but maybe not... probably used Neanderthals or other homo genus, (tho' the Ananasi orchestrated the extinction of the Neanderthals):<br /> The Khara, were-sabretooths\u200b<br /> Mokol\u00e9 remember the Bird Kings (who bred with great flightless birds) and Pouch Kings (who bred with marsupials) surviving on the southern continents for much of the Age of Sleep<br /> The Corax mention a race of were-megatheriums that were slaughtered in the War of Rage<br /> \u200bRumours among the Nagah tell of a breed of humans that could assume the shape of freshwater fishes, who went extinct in the War of Rage<br /> The Shadow Lords remember a breed of werefalcons that were destroyed in the War of Rage<br /> The Fianna remember tribes of wereotters and wereeagles that fell beneath their claws in the War of Rage<br /> Rumours among the Beast Courts tell of breeds of sapient shapeshifting orangutans in the Indonesian rainforests","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 06-17-2023, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T11:23:29-07:00","id":1515407,"title":"","content":"Whoever in charge of the spam-filter must be fired ASAP!<br /> This is insane and anyoing...<br /> So, again...<br /> <br /> <br /> The<b> Insect Races</b>, the <b>Mokol\u00e9</b> and the <b>Rokea</b> not had &quot;homid&quot; , for obvious reasons...<br /> The Mokol\u00e9 after the Lizard Kings (dinosaurs, plesiosaurs, and pterosaurs) re-rolled to Humans<br /> The Drachid form was the near-human form of the Fera before the evolution of hominids - Some believe that the Drachids were the blueprint from which Gaia would derive the idea of humanity.<br /> They were basically Saurian of Dr. Who (and other works) and in theory been able to crossbreed with others, not just the Kings - but only the Ananasi used it really<br /> <br /> During the Age of Kings there lived <b>Ammonite shifters</b> (who were at war with the Rokea and folk became extinct along with their animal kin in the Wonder Work) and <b>Bristlecreeper shifters</b> (whatever a bristlecreeper<i> is</i> ) according Breedbook: Mokol\u00e9 and Rokea<br /> The Rokea say that millions of years ago they were at war with giant, mobile, <b>shapeshifting sea anemones called Qyrall</b>, who served Qyrl (They would ride the leviathans and use Qyrl's gifts of stealth to block out the massive brutes' presence until they were right on top of a slew, then change in to an <i>almost-humanoid</i> shape to do battle\u200b)<br /> The Rokea defeated and apparently eradicated them<br /> <br /> These probably had homid, but maybe not... probably used Neanderthals or other homo genus, (tho' the Ananasi orchestrated the extinction of the Neanderthals):<br /> The Khara, were-sabretooths\u200b<br /> Mokol\u00e9 remember the Bird Kings (who bred with great flightless birds) and Pouch Kings (who bred with marsupials) surviving on the southern continents for much of the Age of Sleep<br /> The Corax mention a race of were-megatheriums that were slaughtered in the War of Rage<br /> \u200bRumours among the Nagah tell of a breed of humans that could assume the shape of freshwater fishes, who went extinct in the War of Rage<br /> The Shadow Lords remember a breed of werefalcons that were destroyed in the War of Rage<br /> The Fianna remember tribes of wereotters and wereeagles that fell beneath their claws in the War of Rage<br /> Rumours among the Beast Courts tell of breeds of sapient shapeshifting orangutans in the Indonesian rainforests\u200b","signature":"","edi